window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["38"]={"https://theconversation.com/humidity-can-make-heatwaves-more-dangerous-its-time-to-warn-australians-about-this-threat-295453":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"e8310068cbe2b25da024d305240d781f629698ad9be16904d9012b49ad6d3925","read":"https://theconversation.com/humidity-can-make-heatwaves-more-dangerous-its-time-to-warn-australians-about-this-threat-295453","bytes":188428,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Humidity can make heatwaves more dangerous. It’s time to warn Australians about this threat","by":[{"n":"Alyson Wright","r":"Adjunct Fellow in Public Health, Menzies School of Health Research"},{"n":"Mark de Souza","r":"PhD Candidate in Sustainable Healthcare, The University of Melbourne"},{"n":"Sharon Campbell","r":"Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Environmental Health Research, University of Tasmania"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T22:18:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It’s the build-up in northern Australia – the time of year when heat and humidity get worse ahead of the wet season. Common phrases such as “going troppo” or “ ",["mango madness","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-12-30/mango-madness/104703932"],"” give a sense of the effects. Tempers fray and tensions rise."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s now ",["emerging evidence","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-026-48668-z"]," that humidity makes heat more dangerous. ",["Humid heatwaves","https://www.aspi.org.au/report/lethal-humidity-and-the-systemic-risks-of-climate-change/"]," – where high temperatures combine with high humidity – are potentially more dangerous than dry heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elsewhere in the world, humid heatwaves are already claiming lives. Over 1,300 pilgrims died in Saudi Arabia in 2024 due to lethal levels of ",["humidity and heat","https://theconversation.com/more-than-1-300-hajj-pilgrims-died-this-year-when-humidity-and-heat-pushed-past-survivable-limits-its-just-the-start-245271"],", while ",["India and Pakistan","https://theconversation.com/too-hot-too-humid-why-the-sustained-heatwave-in-india-and-pakistan-is-so-dangerous-283762"]," have also been hard hit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["recent research","https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GH001562"]," in the Northern Territory found more people came to emergency departments during intense humid heatwaves than comparable dry heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is, we’re not warning people about this combined threat. Australia’s heatwave warning systems focus only on temperature – not on humidity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why humidity matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Intense heat stresses the body. Humidity can make this worse."]},{"k":"p","s":["The human body relies heavily on sweating to regulate temperature. When sweat evaporates from the skin, it removes heat and helps keep the body cool. When ",["humidity is high","https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-02461-6"],", evaporation doesn’t work as well and it’s harder for the body to release heat and stay cool."]},{"k":"p","s":["Humid conditions can boost the risk of heat-related illnesses such as heatstroke, worsen existing heart and lung conditions and put more strain on the bodies of people with chronic diseases."]},{"k":"p","s":["High humidity can also contribute to poor sleep, reducing the body’s ability to recover during prolonged hot periods."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hot and wet conditions also provide optimal conditions for mosquitoes, ticks and parasites, which are vectors for the spread of ",["key tropical diseases","https://theconversation.com/murray-valley-encephalitis-can-be-fatal-with-no-vaccine-heres-how-to-stay-safe-283573"],". Mould, bacteria and viruses are more likely to grow in high humidity, increasing the risk of ",["lung and skin disease","https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24119456"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What we found in the Northern Territory"]},{"k":"p","s":["The top third of the Northern Territory has a monsoonal coastal climate prone to humidity, while the two thirds inland is arid. This means we can analyse and compare humid and dry heatwaves across these environments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study ",["analysed","https://doi.org/10.1029/2025GH001562"]," more than two decades of emergency department data across the NT to see if dry heat or humid heat affected the numbers of people needing emergency care. We used a ",["temperature-based index","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cliser.2022.100315"]," for dry heat and a combined temperature and relative humidity index to determine humid heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["The results were clear. While more people sought emergency treatment during both dry and humid heatwaves, humid heatwaves were worse. Severe and extreme dry heatwaves led to 4.4% more hospital visits, while similar humid heatwaves saw 6.1% more people attending emergency departments."]},{"k":"p","s":["When arid areas of the Territory were hit by humid heatwaves, the effect was even clearer – emergency visits rose 8.7%."]},{"k":"h","s":["Where are the warnings?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In many parts of northern Australia, heatwaves ",["are projected","https://environment.nt.gov.au/media/docs/climate-change-response/state-of-the-science-and-climate-change-impacts-final-report.pdf"]," to become more frequent and intense due to global warming."]},{"k":"p","s":["Every summer, Australia’s Bureau of Meteorology issues ",["heatwave warnings","https://www.bom.gov.au/news-and-media/heatwaves-what-you-need-to-know"]," to give people advance notice of three or more days of unusual heat over day and night. Warnings can be issued for mild, severe and extreme heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["These warnings are vital. They let people prepare for heat and change plans, while health services can boost staffing numbers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem is, these warnings are largely based on ",["temperature","https://www.bom.gov.au/weather-and-climate/specialised-forecasts-and-observations/heatwave"],". Most people can tolerate a 35°C day with low humidity. But a 35°C day with high humidity is much harder for us to cope with."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means the current system may not be warning Australians about a real risk to their health – especially those in tropical and coastal regions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Preparing health services for humid heat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Health services in the NT are often ageing and ",["under strain","https://doi.org/10.1111/ajr.12858"],". Last wet season did ",["significant damage","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-28/katherine-hospital-calls-for-relocation-after-flood-evacuations/106501586"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dry and wet heatwaves will put more pressure on health systems already struggling during ",["extreme weather","https://www.insidestategovernment.com.au/nt-health-confirms-system-wide-pressures-amid-weather-crisis/"],". Even a modest increase in patients will add more pressure on staffing, bed capacity and resources."]},{"k":"p","s":["We’ve long known heat affects some people much more than others. Children, older adults, people with chronic diseases and those in disadvantaged communities are hit harder. In the Territory, ",["low-quality housing","https://doi.org/10.3390/architecture4030041"],", ",["poor access to healthcare","https://doi.org/10.1071/AH21276"]," and ",["outdoor work and recreation","https://doi.org/10.3390/su142113805"]," also boost risks from heat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Time to redefine heatwaves"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s ",["no longer enough","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cliser.2022.100315"]," to define a heatwave using temperature alone. Across northern Australia, humidity directly affects how people experience a heatwave."]},{"k":"p","s":["Climatologists are already ",["exploring ways","https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/adc1e5"]," to include humidity in measures of dangerous heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["To take the threat of humid heat seriously, we need to redefine heatwaves to include humidity and temperature. This will strengthen our ",["early warning systems","https://doi.org/10.1007/s40572-025-00496-5"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On a practical level, we need to prepare our health systems for more demand during severe humid heat, particularly in remote and tropical regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the Top End prepares for another wet season, authorities will focus on the threats of cyclones, flooding and other visible weather threats. It’s time to look at a less visible danger – the combination of heat and humidity."]}],"chars":5084},"https://theconversation.com/us-democrats-win-final-two-senate-seats-coalition-likely-to-easily-win-victorian-election-296423":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6e8040ed0b3280a00ea9a774691821e762ea70ec4dfccfd09d3ed133afad2b96","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-democrats-win-final-two-senate-seats-coalition-likely-to-easily-win-victorian-election-296423","bytes":181636,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US Democrats win final two Senate seats; Coalition likely to easily win Victorian election","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-15T23:05:47Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the United States, Democrats have won the final two undecided Senate seats at the midterms to take an overall 56–44 Senate majority over Republicans. Democrats are likely to win the House of Representatives by 260–175."]},{"k":"p","s":["With 12 days to go until the November 28 Victorian election, a Redbridge poll has the Coalition leading Labor by 57–43 after preferences. The Coalition is likely to easily win a majority of the 88 lower house seats in its own right."]},{"k":"p","s":["The New South Wales election is in March 2027. With NSW using optional preferential voting, the split in the One Nation/Coalition vote in the Resolve poll helps Labor."]},{"k":"h","s":["US Democrats win final two Senate seats"]},{"k":"p","s":["All 435 United States federal House of Representatives seats and 35 of the 100 Senate seats were up for election at November 3 midterm elections. In the 2024 elections, Republicans won the House by 220–215 over the Democrats and the Senate by 53–47."]},{"k":"p","s":["I wrote for ",["The Poll Bludger","https://www.pollbludger.net/2026/11/14/us-mid-term-elections-late-counting-thread-2/"]," on Saturday that Democrat Mary Peltola is certain to win the Alaska Senate contest, defeating Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan. Last Thursday AEDT, the Mississippi Senate contest was called for Democrat Scott Colom, who defeated Republican incumbent Cindy Hyde-Smith."]},{"k":"p","s":["Donald Trump won Mississippi by nearly 23 points at the 2024 presidential election, and the last Democrat to win that state’s Senate contest was in 1982, when southern Democrats were still regarded as racist. The previous Mississippi Democratic senator, John Stennis, was a “ ",["zealous supporter of racial segregation","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Stennis"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["These wins give Democrats a 56–44 Senate majority over Republicans, gaining nine seats at the midterm elections. Seven of Democrats’ gains occurred in states Trump won by ",["double-digit margins","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election#Results_by_state"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the ",["House of Representatives","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/11/03/us/elections/results-house.html"],", Democrats lead Republicans in called races by 256–169 with ten still undecided. Democrats are likely to win by 260–175, the largest Democratic ",["majority since the 1991–93 Congress","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party_divisions_of_United_States_Congresses"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the ",["Cook Political Report’s tracker","https://www.cookpolitical.com/vote-tracker/2026/house"],", Democrats are winning the national popular vote by 56.2–42.3, a 13.9-point margin, compared with a 2.6-point ",["Republican margin in 2024","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I said in the Poll Bludger article that Democrats’ 59.8% of expected House seats is an underperformance of their popular vote margin in single-member systems. Republican gerrymanders probably prevented more losses, although the Republican gerrymander of North Carolina backfired spectacularly."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Redbridge poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["A Victorian ",["Redbridge and Accent Research poll","https://www.afr.com/politics/victorian-coalition-position-strengthens-labor-reduced-to-rump-in-new-poll-20261111-p61d0z"]," for The Financial Review, conducted November 3–10 from a sample of 1,008, gave the Coalition 31% of the primary vote (up one since the early October Redbridge poll), Labor 23% (down one), One Nation 22% (down two), the Greens 15% (down one) and all Others 9% (up three)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition was at its highest since December 2025, while Labor and One Nation were at their lowest since August. The Greens were one point off their October high."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, the Coalition led Labor by 57–43, a one-point gain for the Coalition. Labor led One Nation by 55–45."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor Premier Ben Carroll’s net favourability was down ten points to -28 (47% unfavourable, 19% favourable). Liberal leader Jess Wilson’s was down ten points to +7 (35% favourable, 28% unfavourable). One Nation leader Warren Pickering’s was down three points to -8 (25% unfavourable, 17% favourable). Greens leader Ellen Sandell’s was down one point to -3 (13% unfavourable, 10% favourable)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Wilson had 29% (up one), Carroll 18% (down one) and Pickering 11% (up three)."]},{"k":"p","s":["On whether the Coalition had done enough to deserve to win the next election, respondents gave a -4 net agree score, up four points since October and up 15 points since June 2025. But on whether Labor had done enough, they gave a net -43 agree score, down eight points since October. In the poll before Ben Carroll replaced Jacinta Allan as premier in late July, Labor had a net agree of -50."]},{"k":"p","s":["All recent polls show swings to the Coalition, and the Coalition now has a big lead over Labor as the graph below shows."]},{"k":"h","s":["Victorian Lighthouse poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["The second instalment of the ",["Victorian Lighthouse poll","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/time-for-a-change-coalition-extends-lead-over-labor-as-premier-ben-carroll-faces-losing-his-seat/news-story/5b54bdde2fb1c75512f1ab7a4a448fc3"]," for The Herald Sun gave the Coalition 32% of the primary vote (up one since the ",["Lighthouse poll published November 6","https://theconversation.com/poor-polls-continue-for-both-federal-and-victorian-labor-295756"],"), One Nation 23% (steady), Labor 21% (down one), the Greens 14% (steady) and all Others 10% (steady)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll’s net favourability was up two points to -19, while Wilson’s surged eight points to +17."]},{"k":"p","s":["This poll is being conducted internally by News Corp. No fieldwork dates were provided, but the sample size was 1,351. There will be weekly updates of this poll until the election."]},{"k":"h","s":["Upper house question from previous DemosAU poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["All 40 Victorian upper house members will be elected in eight five-member regions using preferences. A quota for election is one-sixth of the vote or 16.7%, with half a quota enough to give a reasonable chance of election."]},{"k":"p","s":["I previously ",["wrote about the DemosAU poll","https://theconversation.com/labor-slumps-to-new-lows-in-two-victorian-polls-296132"]," that gave Labor just 18% of the primary vote in the lower house. In the ",["upper house","https://demosau.com/wp-content/uploads/DemosAU/vic-poll-nov-2026.html"],", voting intentions were 28% Coalition, 20% One Nation, 17% Labor, 15% Greens, 4% Animal Justice, 4% Family First and 4% Legalise Cannabis."]},{"k":"h","s":["NSW Resolve poll"]},{"k":"p","s":["The New South Wales election is in March 2027. A ",["Resolve poll","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/nsw/the-key-issues-giving-minns-an-edge-four-months-out-from-election-20261113-p61diu.html"]," for The Sydney Morning Herald, conducted with the October and November federal Resolve polls from a sample of 1,100, gave Labor 30% of the primary vote (up one since the September poll), One Nation 26% (up one), the Coalition 23% (down one), the Greens 13% (up two), independents 5% (steady) and others 3% (down two)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a record high in Resolve’s NSW polls for One Nation and the Greens’ highest vote since July 2025, while the Coalition is at an equal record low (tied with July)."]},{"k":"p","s":["No two-party estimate was provided, but ",["analyst Kevin Bonham estimated","https://x.com/kevinbonham/status/2121215834836381937"]," that Labor led the Coalition by over 57–43, with Labor vs One Nation “probably modestly closer”. NSW’s optional preferential voting helps Labor with the One Nation and Coalition vote split."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Labor incumbent Chris Minns had 30% (up three), Liberal leader Kellie Sloane 12% (down three) and One Nation state leader Mike Newman 11% (up three)."]}],"chars":6173},"https://theconversation.com/what-bill-c-39s-loosened-environmental-regulations-could-mean-for-canadians-294851":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"800477aa7241914a3499e03f4c140bd642c39962f36c6598ff0dc5c29ed9b1d0","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-bill-c-39s-loosened-environmental-regulations-could-mean-for-canadians-294851","bytes":183941,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What Bill C-39’s loosened environmental regulations could mean for Canadians","by":[{"n":"Kerry Black","r":"Executive Co-Director, UNU Hub on Empowering Communities to Adapt to Environmental Change, Institute for Water, Environment and Health, United Nations University; University of Calgary"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T14:34:34Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Protests ",["took place","https://globalnews.ca/video/12148696/nationwide-protests-against-bill-c-39-hit-new-brunswick/"]," in cities across Canada today against a proposed bill that some fear could undermine environmental protections as well as the rights of workers and Indigenous communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Canadian government introduced ",["Bill C-39","https://www.parl.ca/legisinfo/en/bill/45-1/c-39"],", the Building Canada Strong Act, in September 2026, with the stated aim of fast-tracking large-scale projects. Hailed as a major advancement by the government, ",["it has also been criticized as a bill that could bulldoze environmental regulations","https://thenarwhal.ca/canada-bill-c-39-environmental-assessments/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has said the proposed legislation is aimed at ",["protecting “economic security.”","https://www.winnipegfreepress.com/breakingnews/2026/09/28/canada-resorting-to-its-tried-and-true-playbook"]," Under the new bill, ",["new “federal economic zones” would be created where projects could be “pre-approved.”","https://thenarwhal.ca/canada-major-projects-economic-zones-proposal/"]," This would provide exceptions to habitat and species-at-risk protections and other federal oversight."]},{"k":"p","s":["What could this new legislation mean for environmental regulations and how could it impact Canadians if passed into law?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Less time for environmental review"]},{"k":"p","s":["In October 2024, the government released a framework for implementing the right to a healthy environment under the Canadian Environmental Protection Act, ",["linking environmental protection directly to human health and well-being","https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/news/2024/10/strengthening-protections-from-pollution-and-the-right-to-a-healthy-environment.html"],". However, Bill C-39 reduces the time period for thorough environmental review."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has touted the bill’s shortened timeline for project approval, ",["compressed to a one-year review","https://mcmillan.ca/insights/publications/bill-c-39-the-building-canada-strong-act-introduces-significant-reforms-to-federal-project-review-and-permitting-process/"],". This allows for quick decisions to be made, and proponents to know whether a specific project will be able to proceed in a shorter timeframe. While this is viewed as a clear advantage, some are warning that the ",["one-year timeline could still be extended and delayed","https://nationalpost.com/opinion/jamie-sarkonak-carneys-one-project-one-year-mirage"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Environmental regulations are not simply environmental protections, they also protect public health. Effective regulations reduce exposure to polluted air, contaminated water, toxic chemicals and climate-related hazards."]},{"k":"p","s":["They help prevent disease, improve quality of life, reduce health-care costs and protect the well-being of current and future generations. ",["Recent evidence shows","https://doi.org/10.1186/s41256-024-00373-y"]," that the health and economic benefits of environmental regulation far outweigh the relative costs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Build first, assess later"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Bill C-39, the government would be able to permit preliminary construction to begin before the Impact Assessment Agency of Canada completes an assessment. This would be the case if the environment minister considers a project to be in the ",["“public interest.”","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/building-canada-strong-c39-expert-environmental-concerns-9.7357425"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Reduced environmental regulations would directly impact the communities within the area of the proposed projects and those downstream. It could mean potential environmental ",["degradation and destruction, as well as weakened habitat protection, before a full assessment can be done","https://www.greenpeace.org/canada/en/press-release/76045/greenpeace-canada-reacts-to-the-introduction-of-bill-c-39-the-bulldoze-nature-bill/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of the proposed “projects of public interest” are in areas of significant ecological importance. Many are situated on or near First Nations territories. Leaders from the Nishnawbe Aski Nation stated they “will not accept this legislation as it stands,” stating they support responsible development but ",["that acceleration of development cannot be at the expense of Indigenous communities","https://www.nan.ca/news/nan-chiefs-reject-building-canada-strong-act/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government is wrong in assuming the choice is either environmental protection or rapid development. Many jurisdictions have shown that ",["projects can move faster","https://climateinstitute.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Regulatory-Reform-NRCAN-and-PCO-Nov.-13.2023.pdf"]," when governments improve co-ordination across departments and agencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["This could include digitizing permitting, establishing clear timelines, conducting strategic planning earlier and eliminating duplication in approval processes. The ",["evidence suggests that delays often arise","https://energy.ec.europa.eu/topics/renewable-energy/enabling-framework-renewables_en"]," from fragmented governance and administrative inefficiencies, not environmental safeguards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pay now, worry later"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bill C-39 also introduces changes to the ",["Fisheries Act","https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/f-14/"]," that make it easier to advance projects that may impact fish or fish habitats. The bill introduces third-party “habitat credits” and fees for minor impacts. Under this model, a third party can engage in habitat restoration and effectively “sell” credits to companies building major projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["The bill would allow companies that damage fish habitat during construction to buy habitat restoration credits from approved conservation groups instead of doing the restoration work themselves. The goal is to speed up project approvals while still requiring companies to compensate for environmental damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Supporters say this could fund larger and ",["more effective habitat restoration projects","https://blog.cwf-fcf.org/index.php/en/cwf-welcomes-government-move-to-protect-fish-habitats/"],", reducing red tape without comprising environmental monitoring. Critics worry it could make it easier for ",["companies to damage fish habitats","https://www.nationalobserver.com/2026/10/01/news/feds-c39-habitat-loss-offsets-questioned"]," as long as they can afford to pay for credits elsewhere, allowing habitat damage to become simply a cost of doing business."]},{"k":"p","s":["Media coverage of Bill C-39 tends to focus on pipelines, mines and regulatory processes. However, it’s also about the air Canadians breathe and the water they drink. It is about the fish we catch and the natural spaces that support our health and well-being."]},{"k":"p","s":["The question is not whether Canada should build new projects or strengthen its economy. It must. The real question is whether it can do so without weakening environmental safeguards that protect communities, ecosystems and future generations."]},{"k":"p","s":["As governments push to accelerate development, Canadians should pay close attention. The consequences will be felt not only in boardrooms and construction sites. They will be felt in rivers, forests and households across the country for decades to come."]}],"chars":5361},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"5e391c5bc6f849158ca4f1c8b9316b246c0fffbace5d4699ff6a2763fcf8edea","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/greece","bytes":114833,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Greece travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-03T11:18:20+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Winter weather in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece can experience severe weather over the winter period, including storms which can lead to flash flooding. For further advice, see the ‘Extreme weather and natural disasters’ section on the ",["Safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Greece’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Greece set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Greek Embassy in the UK","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/the-embassy"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Greece, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period without a visa. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-greece-for-work"]," are different. If you are a touring creative, see ",["details about the Uniform (Schengen) visa","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/visa.html?mission=lon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["For a longer stay, you must ",["apply to the Greek authorities for a national visa","https://www.mfa.gr/uk/en/visa.html?mission=lon"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Greece with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-greece#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Greek implementation of EES"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greek authorities have indicated that they will not collect biometric data (fingerprints and photos) for UK travellers as part of EES. Follow the advice of authorities on the ground. If you are resident in Greece, make sure to show your residence documentation at passport control to ensure you are not registered in EES."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccines, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Greece guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Greece","https://www.aade.gr/en/customs"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques at your point of entry into Greece if you are carrying a value of 10,000 euros or more. You will be asked to complete the relevant declaration forms provided to you by the Customs Authorities. You should request a certified copy of the declaration to keep with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave. You can read further detail on the website of the Greek ",["Independent Authority for Public Revenue","https://www.aade.gr/en/greeks-abroad-non-residents/cash-reserves"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Greece."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several attacks involving explosives and automatic weapons against Greek institutions, shopping malls, banks, media offices, diplomatic premises and the police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 1 July 2026, three improvised incendiary device attacks against the residential properties of Greek political figures killed one person, with four others being injured"]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Political protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greek authorities have increased security at some prominent locations, including tourist sites, due to events in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently a heightened risk of such protests, particularly in central Athens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, stay away from protests and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Strikes and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular strikes, sometimes called at short notice, that can cause disruption to buses, trains, ferries and air travel, as well as road networks and borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations often take place around major squares in central Athens, in particular Syntagma Square. Political demonstrations may take place on certain dates:"]},{"k":"li","s":["1 May (Labour Day)"]},{"k":"li","s":["17 November (anniversary of when student protests against a military dictatorship were put down violently – ‘Polytechnio’)"]},{"k":"li","s":["6 December (anniversary of the shooting of 15-year-old student Alexandros Grigoropoulos)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some demonstrations in the past have turned violent. Avoid demonstrations wherever possible and move away to the last known safe place. Security forces often use tear gas to break up demonstrations, which can harm your breathing and vision."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thefts of passports, wallets and handbags are common on the metro and in crowded tourist places, particularly in central Athens. Do not carry all your valuables in one place and keep a copy of your passport photo page somewhere safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving on holiday, keep your valuables out of sight and lock your vehicle at all times. Always park in a well-lit area or secure car park. Be alert to car crime."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk, especially late at night and around clubs and bars:"]},{"k":"li","s":["save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easier to find at the end of the night"]},{"k":"li","s":["set up a WhatsApp group to keep in touch with others in your group"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep an eye on each other’s drinks to make sure they do not get spiked"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not let a friend walk back to their hotel alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not give a drunk person more alcohol"]},{"k":"li","s":[["see TravelAware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/"]," for tips and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use pre-arranged transport or, where they are available taxi-hailing apps such as Uber or Free Now which supply licensed cabs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Report anything that does not feel right to local authorities or hotel or club management."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Racially-motivated attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of visitors experience no difficulties related to their race, but there have been some racially-motivated attacks, particularly in inner-city areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport, to show to the police if they request identification. Police may not accept a copy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greek police will arrest you for any behaviour they find rowdy or indecent, especially where excessive drinking is involved. Some fancy dress costumes may be regarded as offensive and therefore against decency laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["The courts are likely to impose a heavy fine or a prison sentence if they judge the behaviour to be illegal. Your travel insurance may not cover you if you miss flights because of an alcohol-related arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and underage drinking"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to sell or provide alcohol to anyone under 18, any businesses found doing so can face large fines and possible closure. Bars and nightclubs are not allowed to admit or serve anyone under 18, even if accompanied by an adult. Expect age verification checks at points of sale."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a minor is harmed through excessive drinking, or underage intoxication is brought to the attention of local authorities, parents or other accompanying adults as well as those who supplied the alcohol could face legal consequences under general child protection laws."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Greece have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying goods or services"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law restaurants must provide an itemised bill. Make sure you get a receipt for any goods or services you buy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Carrying weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Offensive items like pepper spray or knuckledusters are listed as weapons in Greece. A knife with a blade measuring 10cm or more counts as a weapon, and you need a special licence for any knife that is not made for domestic, professional, artistic or hunting use."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Greece, and civil unions between same-sex couples have been legal since 2015. The age of consent in Greece is 15, this applies to partners of both the same sex and opposite sex. Transgender people are able to change their legal gender. Anti-discrimination and hate speech laws apply to gender identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public attitudes towards same-sex couples vary throughout the country. Couples showing affection in public may be frowned on, especially in rural areas. Attitudes are generally more welcoming in Athens and on many Greek islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Military service"]},{"k":"p","s":["Men aged 19 and above, born to a Greek national, may have military service obligations, regardless of any other nationality they hold. The authorities can stop you leaving Greece until you complete military service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras or approaching sensitive locations"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to approach or take photos or videos of military installations, vehicles or buildings. The authorities will arrest and have prosecuted those doing so. Border areas are also militarily sensitive. If you visit such areas, do not take photos or videos."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Music festivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care of your valuables at festivals or large concerts. Read the ",["festivals in Europe travel checklist","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"]," for more advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and water sports safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year, people drown in the sea and in swimming pools in Greece."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming pools"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children. Keep small children within arms-reach in and around swimming pools, even if they can swim or there is a lifeguard present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming in the sea. Always supervise children and keep small children within arms-reach."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hidden rocks or shallow depths can cause serious injury or death. Do not dive into unknown water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many organised beaches have a flag system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings. A red flag means you must not enter the water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care and get local knowledge if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further tips on ",["ABTA’s swim safe pages","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"]," and ",["Water Safety on Holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local advice if jellyfish are present."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only book activities at a licensed water sports centre and before you start:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure the paperwork is completed"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask for a safety demonstration"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you know how to call for help"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more advice, see the website for ",["Safe Water Sports","https://safewatersports.com/"],", a non-profit organisation in Greece that aims to prevent accidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad (ATV) biking and mopeds"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year people suffer serious injury and even death due to accidents involving quad bikes. Make sure you get full instructions and training on their use. If you are not experienced with driving quad bikes proceed with caution as you will be sharing the roads with larger and faster vehicles."]},{"k":"p","s":["To help with costs incurred as a result of quad bike incidents you need specific travel insurance as quad biking is defined as an extreme sport and excluded on many policies. Always read the details of your insurance cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["Insurance sold by the hire company usually only provides third-party cover. It’s likely the company will charge you for any damage to the rental vehicle, and you may face arrest if you do not pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check that you hold the correct driving license for the vehicle you are hiring. Provisional licenses are not valid in Greece for driving or hiring any type of vehicle. If you hire a moped, you need a valid driving licence with at least category A1 – ‘light motorcycle’. Choose a category in accordance with your driving licence and age. Category P, which is valid in the UK for driving mopeds up to 50cc, is not valid in Greece."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the vehicle is in good condition. Drivers and passengers must wear helmets before operating quad bikes and mopeds. Failure to do so may invalidate your insurance. If police stop you, they will fine you and take your licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and exploring nature"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when planning a hike or walk, especially during higher temperatures than you are used to. Trails often lack shade and the quality of route markings can vary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ensure that you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your route beforehand, and consider your limitations in distance and difficulty"]},{"k":"li","s":["check weather forecasts and avoid hiking during the peak hours of sun; pack a hat, sunscreen and plenty of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["wear appropriate footwear for uneven terrain and consider taking a map, GPS and a fully charged phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid hiking alone if you can, and always tell someone where you are going and the route you will take"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not light fires as it is both dangerous and illegal due to the high risk of wildfires."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance covers you for extra costs such as mountain rescue service and helicopter evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If an accident happens or if you become lost, call 112 for the emergency services."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Camping and Motorhome travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece has introduced regulations prohibiting camping in tents and the parking of trailers, semi-trailers, camper vans and motorhomes at archaeological sites, seashores, beaches, edges of public forests and in general public areas. Ensure that you use licensed campsites to avoid fines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Greece, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Greece guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/greece/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Greece. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Greece. If you are tested and found to have more than two-thirds of England’s legal limit of alcohol in your system, you could get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic can be busy, fast and chaotic, especially in the larger cities. Local drivers regularly ignore speed limits, including in built-up areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["When walking roadside, take care when crossing the road and if possible use a pedestrian crossing. Drivers do not always stop at crossings, even though they are supposed to. The green pedestrian crossing signal sometimes allows cars to turn right on to a crossing, so cross with caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Emergency alerts and preparedness"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greece can experience extreme natural phenomena such as earthquakes, wildfires, extreme heat and flash floods. To be alerted to events near where you are located in Greece, make sure your mobile phone is set to allow emergency alerts. For instructions on how to do this see:"]},{"k":"li","s":["for iPhones go to Settings > Notifications and enable the ‘Emergency Alerts’ option at the bottom"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Android 11 and higher go to Settings > Notifications > Advanced Settings > Wireless Emergency Alerts"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Samsung devices go to Settings > Apps > Messages > Notifications > Emergency Notifications and enable the ‘Emergency Alerts’ option"]},{"k":"p","s":["This will allow the ",["Greek government’s Emergency Communication Service","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en"]," alerts to reach you. Always keep your phone with you as you will receive alerts according to the location of your phone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consider preparing a grab bag with essentials such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["passports/ID cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["mobile phones and device chargers"]},{"k":"li","s":["money and bank cards"]},{"k":"li","s":["insurance and other important documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["essential medicine and prescription details"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more from gov.uk on what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adverse weather conditions, including floods, can happen quickly. Register for Emergency alerts and follow ",["‘112 Greece’ on X","https://x.com/112Greece"]," for official updates."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of wildfires during the summer season from April to October. Ensure that your mobile phone is registered to receive emergency alerts to be warned of wildfires near your location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. The situation can change quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid starting wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave no litter, especially not glass which is known to start fires"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarettes are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not light barbecues"]},{"k":"p","s":["Causing a wildfire or a forest fire is a criminal offence in Greece – even if unintentional. If you see a fire, call the emergency services on 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you are in or near an area affected by wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow ",["@112Greece","https://twitter.com/112Greece"]," for official updates"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the guidance of the emergency services"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Greek emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact your airline or travel operator who can assist you with return travel to the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, see the ",["Greek Ministry of Climate Change and Civil Protection website","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en/odigies-prostasias/dasikes-pyrkagies"]," (in English)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes and earth tremors in Greece. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["familiarise yourself with safety procedures in the event of an earthquake"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice given by the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Greek emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"p","s":["For further guidance on how to prepare for earthquakes, please visit the ",["Greek Ministry of Civil Protection","https://civilprotection.gov.gr/en/odigies-prostasias/seismoi"]," (in English) and to see, for anywhere in Greece, where your nearest assembly points are located in case of emergency you can visit ",["mysafetyplan.gov.gr","https://mysafetyplan.gov.gr/"]," (map with text in Greek)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 or 166 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Greece","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Greece","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/91/greece"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Greece. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Changes to your routine when travelling, such as later nights, coping with heat and changes to your diet can have an impact on your medication. See the ",["Summer Proof Your Health","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/heat-travel-and-late-nights-how-summer-can-affect-your-medicines-and-how-to-stay-safe"]," campaign for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies across Greece stock a good supply of medicines, but there are strict rules around dispensing certain medicines, including antibiotics. Bring prescription medicines with you and carry a letter from your doctor stating the quantity required during your stay. Keep the medication in the original container with the prescription label. The name on the prescription must match the name on your passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prescriptions for uninsured individuals are only dispensed from:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pharmacies at hospitals"]},{"k":"li","s":["pharmacies registered with the National Organisations for the Provision of Health Services (EOPYY)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to take controlled medicines in Greece, contact the ",["Organisation Against Drugs (OKANA)","https://www.okana.gr/el/information-english"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information, contact the Greek National Organisation of Medicines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 0030 213 2040 395 or 0030 213 2040 285 between 1pm and 2pm on weekdays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: clearance@eof.gr"]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Treatment and facilities are generally good on the mainland, but may be limited on the islands. The standards of nursing and aftercare, particularly in the state sector, is not to the usual standard of the UK. The public ambulance service is basic. There are serious shortages of ambulances on some islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are uninsured, you may not be able to get medical treatment or diagnostic tests from private doctors in Greece, only from public hospitals and primary healthcare centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English. On some Greek islands, local staff in bars or airports may direct you to private first aid or medical centres rather than to the public hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["information if you’re hospitalised in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Greece, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-greece"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["Mental health support for British nationals in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/greece-mental-health-support-abroad/mental-health-support-for-british-nationals-in-greece"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Greece"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Calling 999 from a UK mobile in Greece will automatically transfer you to the Greek emergency services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Greece"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Greece"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Greece"]," in Greece"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/greece-prisoner-pack/information-pack-for-british-prisoners-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece/british-visitors-hospitalised-in-greece"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/greece/british-embassy-athens"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/greece/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Greece","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-greece"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":27968,"change":"New information about winter weather in Greece, including flash flooding ('Warnings and insurance' page)."}};
